 nths\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nThis workshop highlights the accomplishmen
 ts of Black Chicago sculptors with a spotlight on Richard Hunt and Marion 
 Perkins. Hunt\, a world-renowned sculptor and printmaker born in Chicago
 ’s Woodlawn community and raised in Englewood\, became one of the leadin
 g 20th century American artists. During his acclaimed 60-year career\, he 
 was a significant creator of public art in Chicago and across the U.S.\, w
 ith 160 public sculpture commissions in 24 states that included monuments 
 of several notable fig\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com
